^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-08-24 11:18] observe — the npm workspace has a lockfile and root Node range, while internal package manifests are private lockstep shells and most dependency, export, toolchain, and task truth remains centralized at the root.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:19] observe — the editor workspace declares its own compiler and bundler ranges, and current doctor/pack foundations do not yet emit one comparable environment receipt.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:20] define — iteration radius is the dependency, build, test, cache, and conceptual surface a change forces a developer to traverse before receiving a trustworthy result.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:21] decide — distinguish source, manifest, lockfile, runtime, native-addon, ABI, platform, cache, and external-tool failures before attributing a problem to language or application code.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:22] decide — ordinary feature work should have a truthful leaf path plus a root integration path; reducing radius may not skip the public export or generated-consumer product.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:23] taste — onboarding convenience is mature when it supplies a short successful path, an explanation of inherited decisions, and an explicit route for migration or escape.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:33] observe — one identity-free consumer snapshot describes the same recursion dependency as a mandatory sibling checkout in one active guide and as a pure pinned git dependency in another; setup truth needs one checked prerequisite graph.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:34] observe — the same consumer records multi-minute native proof-runtime startup and broad generated-code invalidation for small tasks, making dependency cones and first actionable result more useful than total build time alone.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:35] decide — generate or validate human, machine-facing, and CLI setup instructions against the environment contract; documentation disagreement is a build failure with the conflicting fields named.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:50] observe — the gap-affinity composite build exposed that spw-cli imports spw-runtime while its TypeScript project referenced only spw-seed, causing runtime source to enter the CLI root instead of resolving as a package dependency.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:51] decide — TypeScript project references are part of package truth; the CLI now declares its runtime reference and the seed→runtime→CLI composite build completes from the leaf package graph.
 >>[2026-08-24 12:56] observe — source-route bundle probes measured lite 2.5 KB, parser 68.6 KB, progressive products 64.2 KB, full Seed 313.6 KB, LSP 305.7 KB, and eager CLI 4.1 MB; these are one-tool structural signals, not release budgets or latency claims.
 >>[2026-08-24 12:57] observe — the eager CLI graph pulls about 3.57 MB of TypeScript through authority extraction into every command route; defer the compiler module now, then audit lazy command chunks and public subpaths as package products.
 >>[2026-08-24 12:58] decide — distinguish source export, runtime-load boundary, tree-shakable entry, split chunk, and published artifact in the package audit; a runtime through handle is not a bundle guarantee.
 >>[2026-08-24 13:02] verify — f3ab94eb defers authority extraction until needed; fresh command-registry imports measured 211–324 ms after one earlier 969 ms observation, and a split probe isolates the compiler in its own 3.4 MB chunk.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:34] observe — reconciled against main: ~[1] landed in c46558ff (plan artifacts); outside the list, f3ab94eb (defer compiler loading) and 8d454ad6 (spw-cli tsconfig now references spw-runtime) are on main. ~[2] has not landed: scripts/analyzers has no package-contract audit. Facts for the open questions: all four packages/*/package.json are private at 0.3.0; scripts/release/build-js-dist.ts already bundles bin/spw plus seed (index, parser, lite) and runtime (index, pipeline, substrate, resonance) entries and none for the LSP; extensions/vscode-spw declares esbuild ^0.19.0 and typescript ^5.2.0 against the root's esbuild ^0.27.3 and typescript ~5.9.3.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:34] revise — ?[publication], ?[toolchain_ranges], and ?[entrypoint_matrix] rewritten against those facts so each names the decision it unblocks; ?[task_graph] unchanged. ~[1] pointed at ^[done].
 >>[2026-10-12 15:25] revise — Commits named per the convention in 90c58bbc: 3 landed, 7 planned, 0 dropped.
 >>[2026-10-27 10:19] observe — Public entries moved since the 2026-10-12 reconcile: 900e2b9c added the runtime ./node export and a jsdist entry for it, 603f6b59 added the seed ./reader export, and the parser release (scripts/release/build-parser-release.ts, documented in docs/runtime/md/parser-release.md, now a root) bundles packages/spw-lsp/src/reader.ts and form-reader.ts into its reader and workbench builds. ?[publication] and ?[entrypoint_matrix] restated with these facts; declared shares with parser-releases, which owns that build. Checked at 850077ab: audit_package_boundaries has not landed and no package-contract-audit.ts exists.
}

^["open"]{
 ?[publication]: "All four workspace packages are private and jsdist ships no LSP entry, while the parser release bundles LSP reader code (reader.ts, form-reader.ts) into its reader and workbench builds; should the LSP ever ship as a package, or only inside the VS Code extension and those builds? Decides whether ~[verify_install_matrix]'s matrix includes an LSP pack-and-import smoke."
 ?[toolchain_ranges]: "extensions/vscode-spw pins esbuild ^0.19.0 and typescript ^5.2.0 while the root uses ^0.27.3 and ~5.9.3; converge the extension to the root or keep a tested compatibility matrix? Decides ~[verify_install_matrix]'s extension row and typescript-upgrade-ladder rung A."
 ?[task_graph]: "Can npm workspace scripts meet the measured radius target before a task-graph or cache framework is justified? Answered by ~[measure_dependency_cones]; a no reopens the out-of-scope line on build orchestration in PLAN.md."
 ?[entrypoint_matrix]: "Should the entries build-js-dist.ts already bundles (bin/spw; seed index, parser, lite; runtime index, node, pipeline, substrate, resonance), plus the seed ./reader export only the parser release bundles, be declared the public set, with every other export private until a clean-consumer smoke proves it? Decides ~[leaf_export_smokes]'s export smoke list."
